abstract: >
  PRISM-36K is a benchmark dataset of 36,000 lossless PNG images (512 × 512 px)
  generated by six text-to-image models: DALL-E 2, FuseDream, PixArt-α, SANA,
  Stable Diffusion 1.4, and VQGAN-CLIP. Images were produced from 40
  author-written English prompts (20 short and 20 long, pairwise matched),
  with 150 generations per (model, prompt) combination. The dataset is designed
  for model-attribution research and is released together with 100 reproducible
  train/test splits defined at the prompt level.

keywords:
  - AI-generated image detection
  - model attribution
  - generative models
  - image forensics
  - frequency-domain analysis
  - benchmark dataset

